  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Repeal flawed terror provisions, protect jury trial, and tighten judicial control of any control orders; allow asylum seekers to work and pursue EU‑wide common standards; Single Equality Act and hate‑crime units; extend STV and create a predominantly elected second chamber; strong civil‑liberties framing and decentralisation; strong environmentalism (Carbon Tax, no replacement of aging nuclear plants) and opposition to new Southeast airport expansions; pro‑EU integration and multilateral disarmament focus. TEXT_E: Introduce a points‑based migration system with English for settlement, employer penalties, biometric visas and e‑borders, plus phased ID cards; expand powers against antisocial behaviour, drug testing on arrest with compulsory assessment, control orders and new counter‑terror offences; establish SOCA and restructure for regional/national threats; retain the independent nuclear deterrent; stronger neighbourhood policing and post‑release supervision and tagging.",
